    'female|a||Now that we have seen what four percent a year does to a child''s future health, one question is left: which costs never got booked at all.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    female|a||Our nusinersen base case sits on this line — an illustrative three and a half million kroner per QALY, counting only what the guideline asks us to count.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    female|a||Parents of an untreated child with spinal muscular atrophy hand over hours that no invoice records; book that informal care and the comparator arm gets dearer, so DeltaC shrinks and the ratio falls toward two and three quarter million.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    female|a||The treated child also lives longer, and those added years contain hip replacements, pneumonias, everything unrelated to the disease; book those unrelated future medical costs and the ratio climbs the other way.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    female|a|grave|The two biggest omissions point in opposite directions, because one lands in the comparator arm and the other in the treated one.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    female|a||Lost production, the argument of part three, belongs here to the parents rather than the patient, and shifts the ratio less than their care hours do.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    female|a||And the cost of the assessment itself — the analysts, the submissions, the Beslutningsforum agenda item.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    female|a|soft|It is the thin one.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    female|a||Worth knowing once for the system's own accounts, and worth almost nothing inside this ratio.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    'female|a||So the rule is not count everything: an omission moves the ratio only when it falls unevenly on the two arms.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    female|a||A cost both arms carry alike — the same GP visits, the same travel — cancels inside DeltaC whether you write it down or not.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    female|a||For the boring comparator — a hip replacement at a few hundred thousand kroner per QALY — that same informal-care column is a large share of a small DeltaC, so leaving it out can reorder the whole list.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    female|a||Strip out what cannot move it, and two columns are left.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    female|a||Informal care is the larger of them, and the one a Norwegian base case most often leaves off the sheet — which is exactly why it belongs in its own visible row.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    'female|a||Across all five parts: a cost is the ressursbruk — the resource use — that something else could have had, micro-costed or DRG-averaged, discounted at four percent, and booked even when nobody sends an invoice; what decides the ratio is never the price tag, but the difference between two arms.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    '|a||Next: CEA, CUA, CBA - and why cost-of-illness answers a different question entirely':
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
      voice: en-US-Studio-Q
    'female|a||Nusinersen for spinal muscular atrophy: around seven hundred thousand kroner a dose at list price, six doses in the first year and three a year after — roughly four million kroner in a child''s first year.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
